KEY TEMPORAL PATTERN

Across all four arms:

hit-1 raw Q_margin is approximately 0.28-0.33;

hit-2 raw Q_margin is approximately 0.12-0.14;

hit-3 raw Q_margin is approximately 0.009-0.010.

Thus cooperative margin support loses
more than half its amplitude
before the second adverse decision

and is nearly extinguished
before the third adverse decision.

OWN-MARGIN PATTERN

Across all arms,
mean own aligned M follows:

approximately 0.473 at hit 1;

approximately 0.190 at hit 2;

approximately 0.014 at hit 3.

Therefore repeated opposing evidence
erases support credit
through the entire surviving neighborhood,
not only in cells that already defect.

TOPOLOGY PATTERN

Same-side neighbor count
does not collapse from hit 1 to hit 2.

It is flat or slightly higher.

Examples:

D2 MARGIN:
3.891 -> 4.120.

D2 PHASE:
4.116 -> 4.297.

D3 MARGIN:
3.520 -> 3.779.

D3 PHASE:
3.707 -> 3.960.

Therefore the first major loss
of cooperative field strength
is not caused by neighbors disappearing.

The neighbors are largely still present,
but their margin contributions
have become much weaker.

By hit 3,
same-side neighbor count
has also fallen by roughly one neighbor
relative to hit 1.

Topology loss then compounds
the already severe margin collapse.

DEFLECTION-HIERARCHY PATTERN

At hit 2,
Q_margin still contains meaningful information.

Low-Q cohort cells defect
roughly 50-54%.

High-Q cohort cells defect
only roughly 19-23%.

By hit 3,
that hierarchy has mostly collapsed.

Nearly all surviving cells
have Q_margin near zero,
and defection rates converge
around 68-75%.

This is the strongest evidence
that the third-hit failure
is a cooperative-support extinction boundary.

CAUSAL DIAGNOSIS

The residual 5:3 oscillator
is not primarily caused by
an immediate geometric fragmentation
of the veteran core.

The sequence is:

1. hit 1:
the core remains spatially intact
and cooperative Q is strong;

2. hit 2:
most neighbors are still present,
but repeated opposing evidence
has sharply reduced their M values,
so their cooperative contributions weaken;

3. substantial defection occurs on hit 2;

4. hit 3:
raw cooperative Q is almost zero,
and the topology is now also thinner;

5. the remaining veterans face
the third challenge
without meaningful cooperative support,
and roughly 72-74% defect.

Therefore the causal variable
that needs continuity
is not merely neighbor occupancy.

It is recent evidence-weighted
cooperative support.

NEXT JUSTIFIED MECHANISM CLASS

Do not increase static cooperative gain.

A43 OCCUPANCY_REINFORCE already showed
that sufficiently strong persistent cooperation
can stop oscillation
only by causing pathological rigidity.

Instead test a strictly transient
local cooperative echo:

a committed cell may retain
one epoch of its own immediately previous
raw cooperative Q_margin.

The echo must:

be local;

be commitment-side specific;

last exactly one epoch;

not recursively reinforce itself;

reset on defection / loss of commitment;

use no future evidence;

use no global phase;

and introduce no tunable gain.

A simple candidate is:

Q_raw(i,t)
=
current A43 raw margin-weighted cooperative field.

Q_echo(i,t)
=
Q_raw(i,t-1)
from the immediately preceding epoch
of the same uninterrupted commitment episode.

During local CHALLENGE:

Q_eff(i,t)
=
max(
Q_raw(i,t),
Q_echo(i,t)
).

After the decision,
the trace stored for the next epoch
is Q_raw(i,t),
not Q_eff(i,t).

Therefore an old cooperative field
cannot recursively preserve itself.

It survives for only one additional epoch.

This directly targets the measured pattern:

hit 2 could retain
approximately the stronger hit-1 field;

hit 3 could retain
approximately the hit-2 field;

yet sustained true reversal
continues to drive the stored field downward
with a one-epoch lag.

PLAIN-SPEAK INTERPRETATION

We found the chain reaction.

The second hit does not first destroy
the shape of the core.

Most of the veterans
still have roughly as many veteran neighbors
as before.

What disappears first
is the strength of those neighbors' conviction.

The same neighbors are standing there,
but the evidence credit
they can contribute to one another
has been cut by more than half.

After that weakened second hit
knocks a large group out,
the third hit arrives.

Now the remaining cells have
both weaker neighbors
and fewer neighbors.

Their mutual support is almost gone.

At that point,
being a high-support cell
barely helps anymore,
because almost nobody has much support left.

So the next step should not be
a thicker permanent wall.

It should be a very short memory:

if your neighbors strongly supported you
one epoch ago,
one bad epoch should not erase
all of that cooperative history instantly.

But the memory should not feed itself.

Each epoch replaces it
with what the real neighborhood
actually supported in the previous epoch.

That gives the core
one beat of continuity,
not permanent stubbornness.

NORTH-STAR IMPLICATION

This diagnostic narrows
the distributed-stability problem
from generic cooperation
to temporal continuity
of locally earned cooperative support.

That is a useful developmental property:

a local organization should not forget
its entire recent cooperative structure
because of one transient disturbance,

but it must still dissolve
under sustained contradictory evidence.

